==English==

===Initialism===
{{rfc-header|Initialism}}
{{head|en|initialism}}

# {{label|en|medicine}} {{initialism of|International Normalized Ratio|lang=en}} An indicator of the clotting tendency of blood. Used, for example, to help determine dosage for patients during oral anticoagulant therapy. Outside the normal or target range, a high INR may indicate a higher risk of bleeding, while a low INR may suggest a higher risk of developing a clot.

